### Preserve provider failure state

**Severity:** `medium`

When the provider throws, the catch path leaves only `Value = null`, so diagnostics cannot distinguish a failed load from a genuinely empty icon. Carry an explicit failure bit in the request arguments, set it in `IconProvider.SourceRequestedCore`, and have `IconBox` complete the measurement as `Failed` while clearing the icon.

```suggestion
    public ElementTheme Theme => requestedTheme;

    public double Scale => scale;

    internal bool Failed { get; set; }

    internal IconRequestMeasurement Diagnostics { get; set; }
```

### Reject stale same-key completions

**Severity:** `high`

Theme, scale, or loading refreshes can reuse the same `SourceKey`, so reference equality alone allows an older request to overwrite a newer result. Check the captured request version as well, and report provider failures separately from empty results.

```suggestion
            if (requestVersion != iconBox._requestVersion || !ReferenceEquals(sourceKey, iconBox.SourceKey))
            {
                diagnostics.Complete(IconRequestStatus.Stale, eventArgs.Value);
                return;
            }

            if (eventArgs.Failed)
            {
                iconBox.Source = null;
                diagnostics.Complete(IconRequestStatus.Failed);
                return;
            }

            iconBox.Source = eventArgs.Value;
            diagnostics.Complete(
                eventArgs.Value is null ? IconRequestStatus.Empty : IconRequestStatus.Applied,
                eventArgs.Value);
```
